cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ggah_mod: a layered, differentiable halo-model forward model for galaxies, gas and AGN"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the works it builds on."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Comparat
    given-names: Johan
    email: jcomparat@lpsc.in2p3.fr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9200-1497"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohanComparat/ggah_mod"
url: "https://ggah-mod.readthedocs.io"
license: MIT
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-08"
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - halo model
  - large-scale structure
  - galaxy-halo connection
  - active galactic nuclei
  - intracluster medium
  - JAX
  - automatic differentiation
abstract: >-
  ggah_mod is a halo-model forward model for galaxies, gas and AGN, built in
  six layers whose boundaries are enforced: background cosmology and the
  linear power spectrum, the halo field, the tracer sectors, the one-halo and
  two-halo spectra, the projected observables, and their analytic covariance. Galaxy occupation, hot gas
  and AGN are peers rather than one hosting the others, so a pure gas or AGN
  spectrum needs no galaxy parameters. The same code runs in an accurate mode
  built on a Boltzmann solver and a fast, end-to-end differentiable mode built
  on emulators; the disagreement between them is measured row by row rather
  than assumed.
